#. module: deltatech_pricelist_bulk
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_deltatech_pricelist_bulk
msgid ""
"====================\n"
"Pricelist Bulk Rules\n"
"====================\n"
"\n"
"..\n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"   !! This file is generated by oca-gen-addon-readme !!\n"
"   !! changes will be overwritten.                   !!\n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"   !! source digest: "
"sha256:2605ab9e7a4dbe7de8179285d57e5ea860983e4598f39fb9696fea0df4af9356\n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"\n"
".. |badge1| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/maturity-Beta-yellow.png\n"
"    :target: https://odoo-community.org/page/development-status\n"
"    :alt: Beta\n"
".. |badge2| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/github-dhongu%2Fdeltatech-"
"lightgray.png?logo=github\n"
"    :target: https://github.com/dhongu/deltatech/tree/19.0/"
"deltatech_pricelist_bulk\n"
"    :alt: dhongu/deltatech\n"
"\n"
"|badge1| |badge2|\n"
"\n"
"Adds rules to a pricelist for many products at once and applies the same\n"
"price computation to many existing rules, instead of entering the rules\n"
"one by one.\n"
"\n"
"**Add rules for many products.** The **Add Rules** button on the\n"
"pricelist form, and the **Add to Pricelist** action on the selected\n"
"products (list or kanban of products or product variants), open a wizard\n"
"where you:\n"
"\n"
"- choose what the rules apply on: **Products**, **Product Variants** or\n"
"  **Product Categories**;\n"
"- pick the products, or fill the list with all the products of some\n"
"  categories and of their subcategories (**Add Products of\n"
"  Categories**);\n"
"- set once the **Min. Quantity**, the **Validity Period** and the price\n"
"  computation, with the same options as a standard rule: **Fixed\n"
"  Price**, **Discount** (optionally on another pricelist) or **Formula**\n"
"  (based on the sales price, the cost or another pricelist, with\n"
"  discount or markup, rounding, extra fee and margins);\n"
"- choose what happens when the pricelist already has a rule for the same\n"
"  product, minimum quantity and validity period: keep it, update it or\n"
"  add a new rule.\n"
"\n"
"One rule is created for each product, variant or category. At the end, a\n"
"message shows how many rules were added, updated or kept, and the\n"
"resulting rules open in a list.\n"
"\n"
"**Apply the same formula to many rules.** The **Apply Formula** button\n"
"on the pricelist form (all the rules of the pricelist) and the **Apply\n"
"Formula** action on the selected rules of a rules list change, on all\n"
"the rules at once:\n"
"\n"
"- the price computation; the values of the other price types are\n"
"  cleared, as on the standard rule form;\n"
"- and/or the minimum quantity;\n"
"- and/or the validity period.\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"Enable the pricelists first: *Sales > Configuration > Settings*, section\n"
"**Pricing**, tick **Pricelists** and save.\n"
"\n"
"**Add rules for many products**\n"
"\n"
"1. Go to *Sales > Products > Pricelists* and open a pricelist. The\n"
"   header has the **Add Rules** and **Apply Formula** buttons (**Apply\n"
"   Formula** only when the pricelist has rules).\n"
"\n"
"   |Pricelist form with the Add Rules and Apply Formula buttons\n"
"   highlighted in the header and two fixed price rules of a laptop in\n"
"   the Sales Prices tab|\n"
"\n"
"2. Click **Add Rules**. Choose **Apply On** (products, product variants\n"
"   or product categories) and add the products. To take all the products\n"
"   of a category and of its subcategories, select it in **Add Products\n"
"   of Categories**. Set the **Min. Quantity**, the **Validity Period**\n"
"   and the price computation, then choose what to do with a rule that\n"
"   already exists for the same product, minimum quantity and validity\n"
"   period: keep it, update it or add a new rule.\n"
"\n"
"   |Add Pricelist Rules wizard with five peripherals selected, a Formula\n"
"   based on the Sales Price with 10% discount, rounding to 1.00 and an\n"
"   extra fee of -0.01, and Keep the existing rule selected|\n"
"\n"
"3. Click **Add Rules**. A message shows how many rules were added,\n"
"   updated or kept, and the rules open in a list.\n"
"\n"
"   |Price Rules list with the message 5 rules added, 0 rules updated, 0\n"
"   existing rules kept, and one rule for each peripheral with the same\n"
"   10 % discount on sales price - 0.01 rebate|\n"
"\n"
"4. You can also start from the products: in *Sales > Products >\n"
"   Products*, select the products and use *Actions > Add to Pricelist*.\n"
"   The wizard opens with the selected products; choose the pricelist.\n"
"\n"
"   |Product list with three products selected and the Actions menu open\n"
"   on Add to Pricelist|\n"
"\n"
"**Apply the same formula to many rules**\n"
"\n"
"1. On the pricelist form, click **Apply Formula** to change all its\n"
"   rules, or select some rules in a list of pricelist rules and use\n"
"   *Actions > Apply Formula*. Remove from the list the rules you do not\n"
"   want to change.\n"
"\n"
"2. Tick what to change: **Change the Price Computation**, **Change the\n"
"   Min. Quantity** and/or **Change the Validity Period**, and set the\n"
"   new values. What is not ticked stays as it is on each rule.\n"
"\n"
"   |Apply Formula wizard on the 7 rules of the pricelist, with Change\n"
"   the Price Computation ticked and a Formula based on the Cost with 35%\n"
"   markup, rounding to 1.00 and an extra fee of -0.01|\n"
"\n"
"3. Click **Apply**. All the selected rules get the new computation; the\n"
"   values of the old price type (e.g. the fixed price) are cleared, as\n"
"   on the standard rule form.\n"
"\n"
"   |Pricelist form after the change: the message 7 rules changed and all\n"
"   the rules in the Sales Prices tab with 35 % markup on product cost -\n"
"   0.01 rebate, the minimum quantities unchanged|\n"
"\n"
".. |Pricelist form with the Add Rules and Apply Formula buttons highlighted "
"in the header and two fixed price rules of a laptop in the Sales Prices tab| "
"image:: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dhongu/deltatech/19.0/"
"deltatech_pricelist_bulk/static/description/en/"
"01_formular_lista_preturi.png\n"
".. |Add Pricelist Rules wizard with five peripherals selected, a Formula "
"based on the Sales Price with 10% discount, rounding to 1.00 and an extra "
"fee of -0.01, and Keep the existing rule selected| image:: https://"
"raw.githubusercontent.com/dhongu/deltatech/19.0/deltatech_pricelist_bulk/"
"static/description/en/02_asistent_adauga_reguli.png\n"
".. |Price Rules list with the message 5 rules added, 0 rules updated, 0 "
"existing rules kept, and one rule for each peripheral with the same 10 % "
"discount on sales price - 0.01 rebate| image:: https://"
"raw.githubusercontent.com/dhongu/deltatech/19.0/deltatech_pricelist_bulk/"
"static/description/en/03_reguli_adaugate.png\n"
".. |Product list with three products selected and the Actions menu open on "
"Add to Pricelist| image:: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dhongu/deltatech/"
"19.0/deltatech_pricelist_bulk/static/description/en/"
"04_actiune_din_produse.png\n"
".. |Apply Formula wizard on the 7 rules of the pricelist, with Change the "
"Price Computation ticked and a Formula based on the Cost with 35% markup, "
"rounding to 1.00 and an extra fee of -0.01| image:: https://"
"raw.githubusercontent.com/dhongu/deltatech/19.0/deltatech_pricelist_bulk/"
"static/description/en/05_asistent_aplica_formula.png\n"
".. |Pricelist form after the change: the message 7 rules changed and all the "
"rules in the Sales Prices tab with 35 % markup on product cost - 0.01 "
"rebate, the minimum quantities unchanged| image:: https://"
"raw.githubusercontent.com/dhongu/deltatech/19.0/deltatech_pricelist_bulk/"
"static/description/en/06_reguli_dupa_formula.png\n"
"\n"
"Changelog\n"
"=========\n"
"\n"
"19.0.1.0.0 (2026-11-09)\n"
"-----------------------\n"
"\n"
"- New module: add pricelist rules for many products, variants or\n"
"  categories at once, and apply the same price computation, minimum\n"
"  quantity or validity period to many rules.\n"
"\n"
